From kjh6@psu.edu Fri Dec  1 06:45:40 1995 CST
Message-ID: <199512011244.HAA108240@r02n05.cac.psu.edu>
Date: Fri, 1 Dec 1995 07:44:33 -0500
From: Ken Hoover <kjh6@psu.edu>
Subject: NT 3.51 Firmware upgrade info for SWXCR and AlphaServers

There was a question here a week or so ago from someone
(s.fraser@dem.csiro.au) who was looking for the firmware upgrade necessary
to run NT 3.51 on an AlphaServer with an SWXCR RAID Controller in it.  I am
in the same bind, and here's what I found out after much messing around with
DEC Tech support and banging on the www.order.digital.com web server:

  1)  The part number for the SWXCR RAID controller software disk is
apparently QB-2XHAH-SB ($100 US).  This is a floppy (set?) with the SWXCR
software on it (BIOS version 1.12, Firmware 2.17 and ECU version 3.11).  

  2)  A better option is to get the DEC "AlphaServer AXP Firmware Update CD
v3.3" (DEC # QZ-003AA-E8, $30 US), which apparently includes the SWXCR
firmware on it in a subdirectory as well as firmware for the server itself
and other devices.

  3)  The part number mentioned for the SWXCR firmware in the release notes
(AK-Q6TFC-CA) does not exist -- probably it's been replaced by #1 above.

  4)  DEC apparently is thinking of putting the firmware on the Web server
because someone told me that there is a place holder for SWXCR firmware in
there [I didn't find it, but DEC's web server isn't the easiest to get around].

  This was pulled together from a variety of sources, please confirm this
information with some authority from DEC before acting on it.  I don't work
for or speak for DEC.

  Hope this helps.
                                                        - Ken Hoover

