--Boundary (ID RAOFnEnXyMw45HZDar0vGQ)
Content-type: TEXT/PLAIN; CHARSET=US-ASCII

          
          Just a word on firmware upgrades... The minimum revision that is 
          needed for NTS is (Microsoft Knowledge Base Q126422): 
          
             Model      Recommended Firmware Version
             --------   ----------------------------------
             AXP 150    3.5-4 or later
             AXP 2000   3.6-26 or later (3.7 is preferred)
             AXP 2100   3.6-26 or later (3.7 is preferred)
          
          That rev is pretty old, the current is 4.6 I think. You'd have to 
          have a System that is a couple years old with no firmware 
          upgrades to be out of rev. 
          
          Instead what we have seen is corrupt firmware in 2100's and ECU 
          rev level problems. Corrupt firmware will have symptoms of out-
          of-rev firmware. Wrong rev ECU will tell you to upgrade firmware 
          also (all you really need is the new ECU).
          
          You need v1.8 of the ECU and for corrupt firmware (which may have 
          the same symptoms of wrong rev firmware), press the halt button 
          in and reboot. (This part I don't remember exactly) At the >>> 
          prompt, type CLEAR_ARC_ECU (the syntax may not be correct - check 
          with DEC). This will manually clear the NVRAM. Then you must re-
          install the firmware. A simple 'upgrade' of the firmware will not 
          work - instead, one needs to clear the NVRAM and re-install the 
          firmware.
          
          Just thought I'd pass this on with all of this talk about 
          firmware... Food for thought.
          

