Curt,

When Visual C++ installs it creates all the environment variables to allow you 
to compile from the command line. The env vars are stored in the following file 
for reference:

D:\msvc20\bin>type vcvars32.bat
@echo off
set PATH=V:\MSVC20\BIN;D:\MSVC20\BIN;%PATH%
set INCLUDE=V:\MSVC20\INCLUDE;V:\MSVC20\MFC\INCLUDE;%INCLUDE%
set LIB=V:\MSVC20\LIB;V:\MSVC20\MFC\LIB;%LIB%

Here's an example of command line compiling:

Y:\>nmake

Microsoft (R) Program Maintenance Utility   Version 1.60.5270
Copyright (c) Microsoft Corp 1988-1995. All rights reserved.

        cl -c -W3 -Dtry=__try -Dexcept=__except -Dleave=__leave -Dfinally=__fina
lly -DCRTAPI1=_cdecl -DCRTAPI2=_cdecl -nologo -D_ALPHA_=1 -DWINVER=0x0400 
-DWIN32  -D_WIN32 shutdown.c
shutdown.c
        link /NODEFAULTLIB /INCREMENTAL:NO /PDB:NONE /RELEASE /NOLOGO 
-subsystem
:console,4.0 -entry:mainCRTStartup -out:shutdown.exe shutdown.ob 
advapi32.lib user32.lib libc.lib oldnames.lib kernel32.lib advapi32.lib

Gordon

