From: Bobby Seder <bseder@raven.phs.com>
Subject: Re: your mail
In-Reply-To: <30CF4F60@smtp.nucmed.buffalo.edu>

Nothing.

You can configure this drive (i.e. partitions and formatting) from NT. 
Besides, ARCINST will format (low-level, and it will take a 
REEEAAAALLLLYY long time for a 4gb drive) it as FAT anyway. You don't buy 
anything from doing this from ARCINST. Be advised, NTS 3.51 arcinst is 
buggy, see Microsoft Q138221 in TechNet.

Also, beware 4gb drives are usually double speed (to compensate for the 
size) and they generate extra heat. Consult the company to see if you 
will need an extra cooling fan. Or if it is going in a StorageWorks 
BA-350 box - those have redundant cooling fans.

Hope this helps.

