> 1.  When ever you update the firmware there is mention to use a clear*
> console command after the
>      update and before running the ECU disk.  Is this a must?  Some of the
> readme files talk mention
>      it while others do not.

This is NOT necessary anymore.  Quite a few revs back of the firmware
had some inconsistencies between the SRM and ARC consoles after an
upgrade that the clear* command cleaned up.  This has been incorporated
into the normal firmware upgrade, so the clear* command is not
necessary.  I do not remember exactly what version of the firmware
began upgrading clean, but it was a while ago.  If you need the exact
version, I can dig it up.

This should be cleaned up in the documentation.  I'll point it out to
our documentation folks.  If you want to send me a list of the
documents you found the references to the clear* command in, it might
help.

[...some stuff deleted...]

> In summary I see it as a real bonus to buy the NT kit with firmware included
> during an upgrade so you get all the right parts and in the right order.  I
> know DEC posts between CD versions of firmware on the net.  My problems is I
> have found more than one location for these files.  I also have found more
> than one readme file on how to process the upgrade.  One readme talks about
> using this clear* console command and the other does not.
> 

Well, the "official" firmware area on the net is the one which I
maintain at:
	http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/firmware/

This has been created in conjunction with the folks that create the
firmware CD itself, and is modeled in a similiar structure.

We are trying to coordinate things so that there are not multiple
sources for these files (because it causes exactly this type of
confusion).  I know that the Digital NT folks distribute the ARC
console bits, but I'm not aware of other locations.

Again, it would be helpful it you could give me pointers to the
documents that are conflicting, and also the different locations on
the net you have found for obtaining the firmware.

Hope this helps,
Kevin

